            "reason": "Tyler-approved NVM consolidation; canonical wording preserves the verified path, activation command, version, project set, and pin caveat.",
            "item_id": 1148,
            "query_id": null,
            "new_value": "NVM is installed at `~/.config/nvm/nvm.sh` rather than the usual `~/.nvm/nvm.sh`. In a fresh shell, activate the project runtime with `source ~/.config/nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use 22.22.0` before npm, npx, tsc, Vite, or Playwright work. Node 22.22.0 is a verified machine/project convention for the Corvus frontend, Market-Analytics-Suite, master-corvus, and tyler-vogel-site; individual repositories may not enforce it with an `.nvmrc` or package.json `engines` field. It is not the globally active system Node until NVM is sourced and the version is selected explicitly.\n\nEvidence: neurons 47, 51, 57, 177, 1151, and 1161; live session 019f6e94-2bc3-7393-a5ea-82ce400a1fbc observed `/usr/bin/node` v18.20.4 before NVM activation and successful Node 22.22.0 activation via `~/.config/nvm/nvm.sh`. Tyler explicitly approved deduplication on 2026-07-17.",
